[E0414] Error: cannot borrow `v` as `&var` while a `for` loop walks it
    ╭─[ err/203_range_walk_borrows/main.wip:11:9 ]
    │
 10 │     for x in v.items()[0..2] {
    │              ───────┬───────
    │                     ╰───────── walked here; the loop's binding refers to its elements
 11 │         v.push(x)
    │         ┬
    │         ╰── borrowed here
    │
    │ Note: a `for` binding refers to the element itself, so what the loop walks must not change until the loop ends
────╯
[E0414] Error: cannot assign to `a[…]` while a `for` loop walks it
    ╭─[ err/203_range_walk_borrows/main.wip:18:9 ]
    │
 17 │     for x in a[0..2] {
    │              ───┬───
    │                 ╰───── walked here; the loop's binding refers to its elements
 18 │         a[3] = x
    │         ──┬─
    │           ╰─── assigned here
    │
    │ Note: a `for` binding refers to the element itself, so what the loop walks must not change until the loop ends
────╯
